{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 43, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook, and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. after being dumped by his girlfriend, erica, mark creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy, and mark is eventually called before the harvard administration to face disciplinary action. however, this incident also catches the attention of twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, who approach mark with an idea for a social networking site exclusively for harvard students.\n\nmark agrees to work on the site, but soon becomes obsessed with the project and begins to work on it with his friend eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield. as the site gains popularity, mark and eduardo's friendship begins to fray, and the two have a falling out over the direction of the company.\n\nmeanwhile, the winklevoss brothers become increasingly frustrated with mark's lack of progress on their site, and eventually sue him for stealing their idea. the film's narrative is intercut with scenes from the deposition hearings, where mark is being questioned by lawyers representing the winklevoss brothers and eduardo saverin.\n\nthe social network is a film that explores the complexities of human relationships and the consequences of ambition. the performances are excellent, with jesse eisenberg standing out as the socially awkward but intensely driven mark zuckerberg. the script, written by aaron sorkin, is witty and engaging, and the direction by david fincher is sleek and stylish.\n\none of the most interesting aspects of the film is its portrayal of the darker side of success. mark zuckerberg's rise to fame and fortune is not portrayed as a triumphant or glorious thing, but rather as a complex and often painful process. the film suggests that mark's obsession with facebook came at a great personal cost, and that his relationships with others suffered as a result.\n\noverall, the social network is a thought-provoking and engaging film that explores the consequences of ambition and the complexities of human relationships. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook, or in the broader themes of success, friendship, and loyalty.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028232974000275135}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.10020723193883896}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.008624685928225517}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.18487101793289185}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0005295066512189806}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.39684411883354187}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00977491494268179}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.014305301010608673}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00012265883560758084}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.575939416885376}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.18180598318576813}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -4.970903682988137e-05}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.20398323237895966}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.6422874927520752}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00048792376765049994}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0004297763225622475}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -4.2199197196168825e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0006291079334914684}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -8.34461570775602e-06}, {"token": " begins", "logprob": -0.7941714525222778}, {"token": " with", "logprob": -7.60